Revert and rebase winex11: Pass fullscreen flag to is_window_managed

A regression introduced in wine 10.3 causes the Affinity Sub-Tools panel
to appear above other X11 desktop application windows, including the
Open File Explorer window.

https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/7370/commits

Rebased from the 10.11 patch set onto 11.18. Eleven of thirteen winex11
hunks and two of three Wayland hunks applied as-is; three needed manual
rework:

  - get_window_attributes gained a `DWORD ex_style` local in 11.18, so the
    override_redirect assignment now goes after it.
  - X11DRV_WindowPosChanged was refactored to an `is_managed` local plus a
    make_owner_managed() call. `is_managed` is dropped entirely rather than
    kept: once window_set_managed() is removed nothing reads it, and keeping
    it would leave a set-but-unused local.
  - The Wayland call site renamed `toplevel` to `owner`.
